# Normalise line endings so a Windows checkout does not produce files that break
# inside a Linux container.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The backend entrypoint was rewritten by a Python script on
# Windows, which wrote CRLF, and bash inside the container failed on every line with
# `$'\r': command not found` — a failure that reads as a corrupt image rather than a
# line-ending problem. Shell scripts, Dockerfiles and anything else executed by a
# Linux tool must stay LF regardless of the host.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
